  "result": "Perfect! All 74 tests pass. I've successfully added line discount support with comprehensive validation and calculations.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/errors.js** - Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** - Added discount support throughout:\n   - `validateDiscount()` helper validates discountPercent is a number from 0-100\n   - `createInvoice()` accepts and stores `discountPercent` on input lines\n   - `addLine()` accepts and stores `discountPercent` on new lines\n   - `lineDiscount()` calculates line discount: `lineTotal * discountPercent / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`\n   - `invoiceTotals()` now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n     - `discount` is the sum of all line discounts\n     - `total = subtotal - discount`, clamped at 0 (enforcing the rule that no amount can go below zero)\n\n**Test coverage includes:**\n- Discount acceptance with valid values (integers and decimals like 12.5)\n- Validation rejecting invalid values (>100, negative, non-numeric)\n- Multiple line discount calculations\n- Zero-clamping when discount exceeds subtotal\n- Default discount behavior (0 when omitted)\n\nThe implementation follows the project rule: all computed amounts are clamped at zero minimum.",
